{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובתואל ילד את רבקה", :translit "u-vetuel yeled et rivkah", :gloss "and Bethuel begot Rebecca"} {:he "עד שלא שקעה שמשה של שרה זרחה שמשה של רבקה", :translit "ad she-lo shakah shimmeshah shel sarah zarchah shimmeshah shel rivkah", :gloss "before the sun of Sarah set, the sun of Rebecca shone"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verses: Genesis 22:23 (Rebecca's birth) immediately precedes Genesis 23:1 (Sarah's death)"}], :frame {:text "Genesis 22:23 introduces Rebecca ('and Bethuel begot Rebecca') as the last verse before Genesis 23:1 opens with Sarah's death. The verse sequence itself establishes that Rebecca's arrival preceded Sarah's departure.", :sources ["Genesis 22:23" "Genesis 23:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "שרה מאה שנה", :translit "sarah me'ah shanah", :gloss "Sarah a hundred years"} {:he "שמש וזרח השמש ובא השמש", :translit "shamesh va-zarach ha-shemesh u-va ha-shemesh", :gloss "the sun rose, and the sun shone, and the sun came"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "שרה מאה שנה", :spells "שמש"}], :frame {:text "Ecclesiastes 1:5 describes the sun's cycle: 'The sun rises (וזרח השמש), and the sun comes (ובא השמש).' The Ba'al HaTurim reads the opening letters of Genesis 23:1—'שרה מאה שנה'—as spelling 'שמש,' linking the verse's language to the sun's rising and setting in Ecclesiastes 1:5.", :sources ["Ecclesiastes 1:5" "Genesis 23:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "שני חיי שרה", :translit "shnei chayei sarah", :gloss "the years of the life of Sarah"} {:he "ד\"א", :translit "davar acher", :gloss "another interpretation"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrasts 'שני' (years) with 'ימי' (days); second interpretation calculates Sarah was 90 at Isaac's birth (Genesis 17:17) and lived to 127 (Genesis 23:1), so 37 principal years"}], :frame {:text "Genesis 17:17 records that Sarah was 90 years old when Isaac was born, and Genesis 23:1 states she lived 127 years. Rashi on Genesis 23:1 cites the tradition that at 20 she was as beautiful as at 7, and at 100 as sinless as at 20, and the midrashic reading that she returned to the beauty of youth before her death. The phrase 'ויהיו' ('and they were') is read as indicating her principal years began with Isaac's birth.", :sources ["Genesis 17:17" "Genesis 23:1" "Rashi on Genesis 23:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verses: Genesis 22:23 (Rebecca's birth) immediately precedes Genesis 23:1 (Sarah's death)", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "שרה מאה שנה", :spells "שמש", :letters ["ש" "מ" "ש"], :by :selah, :order :in-order} {:kind :other, :note "Contrasts 'שני' (years) with 'ימי' (days); second interpretation calculates Sarah was 90 at Isaac's birth (Genesis 17:17) and lived to 127 (Genesis 23:1), so 37 principal years", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:07:23.936553811Z", :model "glm-5.2"}